>> title: Western Omelette
>> category: Eggs
>> tags: eggs, ham, peppers, breakfast, skillet
>> counters: Diner, One Pot
>> aka: denver omelette, Denver omelet, western omelet, denver omelette sandwich, western sandwich
>> servings: 1
>> time: 15 min
>> washing-up: the nonstick skillet, a bowl to beat the eggs in

>> step: sweat 3 min, until the pepper softens
Sweat @cooked ham{2%oz}(60 g; in 1/4-in dice), @yellow onion{2%Tbs}(20 g; diced) and @green bell pepper{1/4%cup}(35 g; diced) in @unsalted butter{1%tsp}(5 g) in an #8-in nonstick skillet{} over medium heat ~fry{3%min}, until the pepper loses its squeak.

>> step: beat until no white streaks show
Beat @eggs{3%large}(150 g), @water{1%Tbs}(15 mL), @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} and @black pepper{1/8%tsp} with a fork until no streaks of white are left.

>> step: set 2 min, stirring then still
Set @&(~1)beaten eggs{} in @unsalted butter{1%Tbs}(14 g) over medium-low heat ~fry{2%min}, stirring small circles for the first twenty seconds and then leaving it alone, until the top is barely wet.

>> step: fill, fold in thirds, slide out
Fill @&(~1)set eggs{} with @&(~3)sweated ham and peppers{} and @shredded cheddar{1/4%cup}(30 g) down the middle, fold it in thirds over the filling, and slide it out onto the plate seam side down.
